    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0908" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894c.20/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-27T16:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1934—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. Reference Dairen’s despatch to you dated June 29, 1934,<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d720-f1"/> subject “Foreign Firms Requested to Contribute towards
                    Air Defense of Dairen.”</p>
                <p>Please ascertain from Vincent<anchor n="10" xml:id="d720-f2"/> the present status
                    of this matter and report by telegraph as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d720-f1" n="9" xml:id="d720-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d720-f2" n="10" xml:id="d720-f2-content">
                <p>John Carter Vincent, Consul at Dairen.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
